    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Don Sebastian Juan Dominguez was a mortal rancho owner near the pueblo of Los Angeles who fled his own home in 1828 after the frenzying Toreador elder Christopher Houghton slaughtered his family and made him a ghoul. For over a century Don Sebastian ruled Los Angeles as Christopher's unwitting \"front man,\" secretly Blood Bound and utterly loyal, crowned Prince by his hidden master in 1870. Under his rule the city became a magnet for decadent Kindred, and his careless indulgence of Toreador poseurs and casual cruelty toward the growing anarch population &mdash; including a savage beating of Jeremy MacNeil in 1943 &mdash; finally triggered the 1944 Revolt. Salvador Garcia is publicly credited with killing Don Sebastian in single combat, but Christopher Houghton himself struck the actual killing blow.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>(For flashback/historical use.) Regal, indulgent, casually cruel to anarchs and utterly devoted, without knowing why, to his unseen master's wishes.</p>",
    "notes": "Deceased (destroyed in the 1944 Revolt). Included as a historical/flashback NPC: a ghoul who ruled as Prince for over a century without ever realizing he was a puppet. npcType is 'ghoul.'",
    "npcType": "ghoul"
